  "improvement": {
    "owning_skills": [
      "stream-processing-design"
    ],
    "mechanism": "Extend stream-processing-design with completeness and commit-order checks for CDC transaction buffers. Transaction END markers, expected event counts per table, unique event identity and transaction order establish different facts. Completed later transactions may need to wait for earlier transactions. The destination still needs an atomic transaction. Schema evolution must also cover operator state, historical replay and sink schemas, independently of registry compatibility.",
    "reading_and_contract_limits": "Both selected bodies were read completely. The transaction buffering implementation is experimental and was not executed. Large transactions can exceed broker message limits; a naive in-memory SMT has unbounded memory and no buffer fault tolerance. Debezium transaction metadata and DDL support depend on connector and configuration. Flink CDC synchronization modes and supported connectors need current version verification.",
    "discriminating_case": "Deliver a later small transaction before an earlier large one completes, and duplicate one CDC row while its END marker expects two unique rows. Require unique completeness, source commit order, persisted recoverable buffering and atomic sink application. Repeat with a schema rename and historical event replay to expose registry versus state and sink compatibility."
  },
